:: Plane Explore
<<applyLocationEffects>>
You slowly pry open the plane's door with a nearby steel rod and enter. Dozens of lurkers screech and skitter out as you enter. As expected there's not much to scavenge. The interior is pretty overgrown and nothing worthwhile can be found.
<br><br>
However upon searching within the surrounding area you find a small stone makeshift home. Inside you find nothing more than a few ripped sheets of paper.
<br><br>
<<if $prutiquest is 1>>
    <<link [[Search the wreckage for Pruti (0:10)|Wreckage Vial]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
    <br>
<</if>>
<<schoolicon "library">><<link [[Read the notes (0:10)|Notes 1]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Back (0:05)|Misland]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>

:: Notes 1
<<applyLocationEffects>>
The crash was brutal. I may be the only survivor, but it's hard to say. My companion is most certainly dead and buried somewhere under this mess. The creature is probably also deceased, though not because of anything I did. But that is neither here nor there; at the moment my only concern is surviving this terrible storm and whatever might come out of it.
<br><br>
It began when I heard a strange noise. It sounded like nothing I had ever experienced before and at first I thought something might be wrong with me, that maybe I needed some water or food, since my mouth was so dry, but then I realized what it must be— it was music. A strange, haunting tune. There are no instruments, no people playing; it was like hearing a radio broadcast coming through the air or perhaps someone on an intercom from another room. It was soft, almost inaudible and it didn't go away until the thunder came, drowning it out completely.
<br><br>
As I got up to see where the sound came from, I tripped over something on the floor that was lying right in front of me, which made me look down. And there he was, my companion, dead and cold as death, though the rain seemed to bring life back into him somehow. I can still hear that song faintly. I have no idea what it means, though I suspect there is some meaning, if only I knew what to listen for.
<br><br>
<<schoolicon "library">><<link [[Continue reading the next page (0:10)|Notes 2]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Back (0:05)|Misland]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>

:: Notes 2
<<applyLocationEffects>>
I'm beginning to doubt my sanity. What does the music mean? Is it just the sounds I'm hearing or does it represent something else? It's so strange. When the weather gets bad, it starts sounding more beautiful and when the weather clears, the sound becomes sad, as though some great tragedy took place when the sun went away. The rain seems to be making it worse too. Now it's raining even harder than it was yesterday, and though I have shelter, I'm worried about whatever lies outside in the darkness. Maybe the storm will pass in time for tomorrow— the weather doesn't seem to last forever. At least the rain has stopped for now, allowing me a bit more visibility, though everything is still covered in fog.
<br><br>
<<schoolicon "library">><<link [[Continue reading the next page (0:10)|Notes 3]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Back (0:05)|Misland]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>

:: Notes 3
<<applyLocationEffects>>
Still alive! Though, to tell you the truth, I don't feel too good. The fever seems to be getting worse and this cough won't stop. Whatever is growing inside of me isn't doing me any favors either— I think-
<br><br>
The page is ripped beyond this point and unreadable.
<br><br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Back (0:05)|Misland]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>

:: Hut Explore
As expected there's not much open first glance. The shattered window covers the floor. You're shocked to find an old dusty skeleton in the back. One of its legs are missing.
<br><br>
Beside the skeleton there's an old bloody notebook and pen.
<br><br>
<<schoolicon "library">><<link [[Read the notes (0:10)|Notes 4]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Take a rest (1:00)|Hut Rest]]>><<pass 60>><<set $tiredness -= 200>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Back (0:05)|Misland]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>

:: Hut Rest
You lie down in the old musty cabin trying to pay the skeleton no mind, the bed is rough and pains your back but you can manage out an hour of rest before having to get up. Better than nothing.
<br><br>
<<link [[Back|Hut Explore]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>

:: Notes 4
I don't know what day it is anymore, but I must have slept through at least three days because of the way I feel. This sickness has gotten worse and it feels like whatever disease I caught is trying to eat its way out.
<br><br>
This might sound insane, but I believe the creature has found me. If not today, then soon; maybe even right now. For there are times when it comes to a door I left open, looking through the glass with eyes that are so cold it chills me to my very soul. Or perhaps they see something else, though I doubt it.
<br><br>
If I survive, if I ever make it back to civilization, I'm going to have to warn people of what I've seen. Not everyone is going to believe me— I'm sure most will dismiss it as the delusions of a madman or even accuse me of being drunk. But I will do it, I swear to you. I'll put together some kind of evidence. Something tangible.
<br><br>
I have to write, though; it's my only link to sanity and reason. It allows me to forget, even if just for a few hours. The words seem to fill an empty hole that's been growing inside of me since I woke up in this terrible place. If anything, they help me find myself again. And maybe if anyone ever finds these pages, they can use them as proof— proof that this really happened and that something must be done about it before someone else becomes the next victim.
<br><br>
<<schoolicon "library">><<link [[Continue reading the next page (0:10)|Notes 5]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Back (0:05)|Misland]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>

:: Notes 5
Oh God. Please make it stop, please make it-
<br><br>
It's almost here! He's coming for me. His fingers claw at the glass like it's alive, like he's trying to get through it so badly I can hear him breathing. He's looking in on me, just like I'm watching him, and there's nothing I can do but wait for the end to come. The song has changed; the tune has faded away, leaving me to wonder what it means, but it was beautiful. So hauntingly beautiful that I wish I could listen to it again. I think I heard it once more before he arrived.
<br><br>
He's almost through the glass now. I can see the dark shadow of his arm as it reaches up, as if his fingers are grasping for something. He's coming closer, and though I don't know how, somehow I'm sure it's only because he's drawn by my voice— by the sound of my thoughts and memories. It's too late. There is no escaping this creature now, not after he's reached into this room. He knows where I am and he'll follow me anywhere I go— I've tried to escape from the house, but he follows me every step of the way. I don't want to die.
<br><br>
And so, I write one last note—though I'm certain no one will ever read it or understand it, this journal has helped me through some of the worst days I have had in recent memory.
<br><br>
<<schoolicon "library">><<link [[Continue reading the next page (0:10)|Notes 6]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Back (0:05)|Misland]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>

:: Notes 6
The page is illegible, the words are scribbled beyond comprehension and dried blood obscures the page.
<br><br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Back (0:05)|Misland]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>

