:: Misland Shrine
The village's shrine is a small and humble structure, nestled within the trees alongside the oasis. The shrine is dedicated to the divine entity that the villagers worship, and it serves as a place of prayer, meditation, and spiritual healing.
<br><br>
The shrine's exterior is made of simple stone, with a small opening to allow the villagers to enter and exit. Inside, there is a central altar, upon which the villagers place offerings and flowers in honor of their deity. The altar is adorned with small statues and symbols of the deity, and the air is filled with the delicate scent of incense.
<br><br>
<<wolficon>><<link [[Pray|Shrine Pray]]>><<set $phase to 1>><</link>>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Leave (0:05)|Desert Village]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>

:: Shrine Pray
<<if $phase is 1>>
	You sit on a mat and bow your head.
	<br><br>
<<elseif $phase is 2>>
	You pray for salvation. Your thoughts drift to your hopes for the future, and how things could be better.
	<br><br>
	An hour passes, and you feel less burdened.
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<link [[Pray for salvation (1:00)|Shrine Pray]]>>
	<<pass 60>><<set $phase to 2>>
	<<if $purity gte ((1000 / 7) * 7)>>
