:: Ant Colony Clean
<<effects>>
You focus on cleaning up after the ants, hoping to blend into the background.
<<set $rng to random(1, 3)>>
<<if $rng gte 3>>
    They spill saliva on the floor. You sweep up after them.
<<elseif $rng gte 2>>
    You take a moment to clean up the rancid moldy boards.
<<else>>
    You sweep up crumbs from the floor.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Ant Slavery]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Ant Colony Dig
<<if $antdig gte 10>>
    You return to the soft tunnel and keep digging. All of a sudden, you hear the sound of sand trickling through the stone. You step back as you realize the roof is about to collapse. You quickly climb up, hoping to escape the oncoming rocks and sand. As you reach the surface, you take a deep breath, grateful to be out of the tunnels. You know you have to make your way to a safer place as soon as possible.
    <br><br>
    <<link [[Next|Misland]]>><<set $islanddistance to 10>><</link>>
<<elseif $antdig gte 8>>
    You return to the soft tunnel and keep digging. You start to hear the sound of sand shifting through the stone. It's coming from somewhere up ahead. You're not entirely sure what this means, but you know that you're close to finding something. You press on, determined to keep digging until you find a way out. You'll have to trust your intuition and hope that you're on the right track.
    <br><br>
    <<link [[Next|Ant Slavery]]>><<set $antdig += 1>><</link>>
<<elseif $antdig gte 6>>
    You return to the soft tunnel and start digging again. You find that the wall is softer here, and you can easily make good progress through the sandstone. You work as quickly as you can, but you're still aware of the risks of being caught. You'll have to keep a low profile and be careful not to make too much noise.
    <br><br>
    <<link [[Next|Ant Slavery]]>><<set $antdig += 1>><</link>>
<<elseif $antdig gte 3>>
    You return to the soft tunnel and dig as long as you can. The tunnel is a bit longer than when you first found it, but you have no idea how far you have left to go. You're worried about the risk of being discovered, but you're also desperate to find a way out.
    <br><br>
    <<link [[Next|Ant Slavery]]>><<set $antdig += 1>><</link>>
<<elseif $antdig gte 1>>
    You return to the soft tunnel and start digging away at the wall. Your progress is slow, and you're not sure how long you can keep this up. You're worried that the guards might find this tunnel if you spend too much time digging. They might be preoccupied for now, but a dedicated search would reveal your hiding spot quickly. You'll have to work fast and be cautious.
    <br><br>
    <<link [[Next|Ant Slavery]]>><<set $antdig += 1>><</link>>
<<elseif $antdig is 0>>
    Searching these labyrinthine tunnels is a daunting task, and you wonder if you'll ever find a way out. The tunnels stretch deep into the rock, some no more than a few feet across, while others seem to extend for an eternity before twisting back on themselves. You're walking through one tunnel when the sand catches your eye - it seems softer, as if it were disturbed. Could this be a way up and out of here?
    <br><br>
    <<link [[Next|Ant Slavery]]>><<set $antdig += 1>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Ant Passout
The world seems to fade in and out as you're jostled around. Suddenly, you jolt up, feeling a strong burning sensation in your stomach. You're unable to hold back and vomit up odd-looking pieces of meat and green fluid. As the ants surround you, curious about the new figure in front of them, you make eye contact with them. Upon seeing you are awake, they quickly return to their work and leave you alone, feeling slightly ill. You take a deep breath, trying to collect yourself and make sense of what happened.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Ant Slavery]]>><</link>>

:: Desert Search
<<upperwear 79>>
<<lowerwear 71>>
You search the dunes for anything that could be considered clothing. You only find an old faded cloth that you rip into rags.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Misland]]>><</link>>

:: Misland Mouseear
<<effects>>
You search the forest for seeding flowers. You find a beautiful bunch of mouse-ear you could probably cultivate back home.
<br><br>
<span class="gold">You can now grow mouse-ear.</span>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Misland]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Misland Crowfoot
<<effects>>
You search the soft powdery snow for any plants. You extract the flowers carefully and pull out a glacier crowfoot.
<br><br>
<span class="gold">You can now grow glacier crowfoot.</span>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Misland]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Desert Dock Shops
Shops line the sturdy pier. The dock looks a lot more developed than the surrounding village, showing it was most likely built by travellers from the surrounding nations. Within the shops you see various bits and bobs from places far and wide. Besides the obvious British influence, you spy various imports from Arabia and India and although rare, you even spot one or two importers from east asia. This seems like a fairly common stopping point for refueling and trading for rare trinkets.
<br><br>
<<stallicon "open">><<link [[Visit the clothing shops|Misland Clothing Shop]]>><<set $specialClothes["classicserafuku"] to "unlocked">><<set $specialClothes["serafuku"] to "unlocked">><<set $specialClothes["gakuran"] to "unlocked">><<set $specialClothes["sailorribbon"] to "unlocked">><<set $specialClothes["spiritmask"] to "unlocked">><</link>>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Back|Misland Dock]]>><</link>>

:: Wreckage Vial
Following Pruti’s directions, you dig through the rusted sheets of metal and crumbled hull in search of anything. After a while of digging, you find a small vial dripping some strange fluid that shifts hue between pale and purple. This is almost definitely what Pruti would have wanted.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Plane Explore]]>><<set $prutiquest to 2>><</link>>

:: Ant Nest
You arrive in a room full of pulsating egg sacks. Dark shadows swirl inside the transparent shells. This seems to be the room the queen's young are stored. It would probably be wise to leave while you can.
<br><br>
<<if $prutiquest is 3>>
    <<link [[Take a sample from one of the egg sacks|Pruti Egg Sample]]>><</link>>
<</if>>
<br>
<<link [[Back|Ant Colony Shrine]]>><</link>>

:: Pruti Egg Sample
You approach a large pulsating egg sack. Something squirms within the egg beside the developing ant. You insert the needle into the flesh and extract a fluid that seems to be a mix of a greenish blood and the same pale purple mix you found on the plane. Before you can do anything, the egg splits and a clutch of lurkers flow onto the floor. They quickly begin to leap at you without warning.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Egg Struggle]]>><<set $struggle_start to 1>><<set $eventskip to 2>><<set $prutiquest to 4>><</link>>

:: Egg Struggle
<<effects>>

<<if $struggle_start is 1>>
    <<struggle_init>>
	<<set $struggle.creature to "lurker">>
	<<struggle_creatures 3 2>>
	<<set $combat to 1>>
	<<controlloss>>
	<<violence 1>>
	<<molested>>
	<<set $struggle.mouth.creature to "lurker">>
	<<set $mouthuse to "struggle">><<set $mouthstate to "struggle">><<set $struggle.enemy[0].location to "mouth">>
	<<unset $struggle_start>>
<</if>>

<<struggle>>

<<if $struggle.done gte $struggle.number>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Egg Struggle Finish]]>><</link>></span>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Egg Struggle]]>><</link>></span>
	<br>
<</if>>


:: Egg Struggle Finish
<<effects>>

The creature falls to the ground. You stagger on the slippery nest floor before catching your breath and moving on.
<br><br>

<<clotheson>>
<<endcombat>>

<<link [[Next|Ant Nest]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Caldera Explore
You are deep in the depression of the island's caldera. Heavy fog obscures sight and blistering winds prick your skin. Getting lost in here could spell the end for you if you do not keep your bearings straight.
<br><br>
<<if $calderanorth is -2 and $calderawest is 3>>
    As you stumble in the frozen wasteland, you stumble upon a deep cave that you hadn't seen in the storm, this might be a good place to rest.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if $calderanorth is -2 and $calderawest is 3>>
    <<link [[Pull yourself into the protection of the cave (0:05)|Caldera Cave]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
    <br>
<</if>>
<<if $calderanorth is 0 and $calderawest is -5>>
    <<link [[Climb out of the caldera (0:05)|Misland]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
    <br>
<</if>>
<<if $calderanorth lt 5>>
    <<link [[Make your way north (0:05)|Caldera Explore]]>><<pass 5>><<set $calderanorth += 1>><</link>>
    <br>
<</if>>
<<if $calderanorth gt -5>>
    <<link [[Make your way south (0:05)|Caldera Explore]]>><<pass 5>><<set $calderanorth -= 1>><</link>>
    <br>
<</if>>
<<if $calderawest lt 5>>
    <<link [[Make your way east (0:05)|Caldera Explore]]>><<pass 5>><<set $calderawest += 1>><</link>>
    <br>
<</if>>
<<if $calderawest gt -5>>
    <<link [[Make your way west (0:05)|Caldera Explore]]>><<pass 5>><<set $calderawest -= 1>><</link>>
    <br>
<</if>>

:: Caldera Cave
You crawl down a crack in the ice into a damp icy cave.
<br><br>
<<if $prutiquest is 5>>
A deep guttural growl comes from deeper in.
<br><br>
<</if>>
<<link [[Rest|Caldera Cave Rest]]>><<pass 60>><<set $tiredness -= 200>><</link>>
<br>
<<if $prutiquest is 5>>
<<link [[Descend even deeper into the cave|Caldera Bear]]>><</link>>
<br>
<</if>>
<<link [[Leave|Caldera Explore]]>><</link>>

:: Caldera Cave Rest
You lay your head on the ice and attempt to rest, it is quite a bit warmer inside and the ice melts slightly, leaving you uncomfortably wet. You manage to close your eyes and sleep for only an hour before your body groans in pain and demands you get up.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Caldera Cave]]>><</link>>

:: Caldera Bear
<<beastNEWinit 1 bear>>
As you walk deeper into the ice cave, you slip on a slab of melty ice. You slide down into a large central chamber. Before your eyes, in the darkness, you see the lumbering form of a <<beasttype>> but… something is wrong. Its eyes are glazed over and it seems almost passive. Its skin bulges strangely and seems to almost pulsate. Suddenly without warning, the <<beasttype>> pauses and its eyes come to life with aggression. Tentacles burst from under its skin and it charges, barreling right toward you.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Caldera Bear Rape]]>><<set $molestationstart to 1>><</link>>

:: Caldera Bear Rape
<<if $molestationstart is 1>>
	<<set $molestationstart to 0>>
	<<controlloss>>
	<<violence 1>>
	<<neutral 1>>
	<<molested>>

	<<beastCombatInit>><<set $enemyhealthmax to 600>><<set $enemyhealth to 600>><<set $enemyarousalmax to 1000 * $beastarousalmult>>
    <<makeAbomination _wraithtentacles 6 "tentacle" "pale" true>>
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<set $enemytrust -= 100>><<set $enemyanger += 100>>
<<effects>>
<<effectsman>>

<br>
<<beast $enemyno>>
<br><br>
<<stateman>>
<br><br>
<<actionsman>>

<<if _combatend>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Caldera Bear Finish]]>><</link>></span><<nexttext>>
<<else>>
	<span id="next"><<link [[Next|Caldera Bear Rape]]>><</link>></span><<nexttext>>
<</if>>

:: Caldera Bear Finish

<<effects>>

<<if $enemyarousal gte $enemyarousalmax>>
	<<beastejaculation>>

	The <<beasttype>> returns to its abode.

	<<tearful>> you retreat to gather yourself.
	<br><br>

	<<clotheson>>
	<<endcombat>>

	<<link [[Next|Caldera Cave]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif $enemyhealth lte 0>>
	The mighty <<beasttype>> collapses with a thud. It stills yet the tentacles within it continue to writhe and squirm. As you approach, you manage to dodge as a tentacle narrowly misses you before it falls to the ground, disconnecting from the <<beasttype>>.
	<br><br>

	<<tearful>> you collect the now still lurker and retreat from the dark chamber.
	<br><br>

	<<clotheson>>
	<<endcombat>>

	<<link [[Next|Caldera Cave]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><<set $prutiquest to 6>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	The mighty <<beasttype>> collapses with a thud. It stills yet the tentacles within it continue to writhe and squirm. As you approach, you manage to dodge as a tentacle narrowly misses you before it falls to the ground, disconnecting from the <<beasttype>>.
	<br><br>

	<<tearful>> you collect the now still lurker and retreat from the dark chamber.
	<br><br>

	<<clotheson>>
	<<endcombat>>

	<<link [[Next|Caldera Cave]]>><<set $eventskip to 1>><<set $prutiquest to 6>><</link>>
